# Frontend Performance Rules

## Related Rules
- @frontend-rules.mdc for general frontend guidelines
- @frontend/core/state-management.mdc for state-related performance
- @frontend/core/testing.mdc for performance testing

## Overview
This document defines the rules and best practices for maintaining optimal performance in Ruby on Rails frontend applications.

## Performance Principles

### 1. Asset Pipeline
- Use proper asset precompilation
- Implement proper asset organization
- Use appropriate asset compression
- Implement proper asset caching
- Use CDN for static assets

### 2. Caching Strategies
- Implement Russian Doll caching
- Use fragment caching
- Implement proper cache keys
- Use cache digests
- Implement proper cache expiration

### 3. Database Optimization
- Use proper database indexing
- Implement eager loading
- Use counter caches
- Implement proper database queries
- Use database views where appropriate

## Implementation Guidelines

### Asset Pipeline
```ruby
# Good
# config/initializers/assets.rb
Rails.application.config.assets.precompile += %w( application.js application.css )

# Bad
# No asset precompilation configuration
# No asset organization
```

### Caching Implementation
```ruby
# Good
<% cache [@product, @user] do %>
  <%= render @product %>
<% end %>

# Bad
<% cache @product do %>
  <%= render @product %>
  <%= render @user %> # Mixed concerns
<% end %>
```

## Performance Monitoring
- Use New Relic or similar tools
- Monitor database queries
- Track response times
- Monitor memory usage
- Track cache hit rates

## Testing Requirements
- Load time testing
- Database query testing
- Cache effectiveness testing
- Asset loading testing
- Memory usage testing

## Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Not using proper caching
- N+1 queries
- Not precompiling assets
- Not using CDN
- Not implementing proper database indexing

## Validation Checklist
- [ ] Asset pipeline configured
- [ ] Caching implemented
- [ ] Database optimized
- [ ] Performance monitoring in place
- [ ] Tests cover performance scenarios
- [ ] Response times meet targets
- [ ] Memory usage optimized
- [ ] Cache hit rates monitored
